2. **CodeQL and the push.** You push the branch only. **Tuesday reads the PR's checks and lands it after the gate and CodeQL and the checks are green; never bypass, never dismiss an alert, never comment on the PR, never re-run a check as a clearance.** Push once, plainly, a NEW branch, under the shared git lock (atomic `mkdir`, read any holder first, release by a MOVE of your own only; it wraps the ref write only, never a build or a test), under `/bin/bash`: `git -C '<wt-b758-fix>' push origin HEAD:refs/heads/b758/mps-csproj-tie-comment`. **Never `--force`, `--force-with-lease` or a `+refspec`, never another ref name, never a second push without Tuesday.** Read it back with `ls-remote` (the branch equals your sha; retry up to 2 minutes). Then `gh -X GET api repos/datasecau/MPS-Commercial-Calculator/commits/<sha>/check-runs`: state the counts and which are pending or failed; there is no PR, so expect 0 and say CodeQL NOT SCANNED, never green.
